  "facts": [
    "Calendar arithmetic (lib/days.tsx, checked at module load): Jan 1 1996 to Dec 31 2025 is 10,958 days ('thirty years is almost eleven thousand days'). March 14, 2011 was a Monday (computed from the calendar, not typed).",
    "HSAM (highly superior autobiographical memory, a.k.a. hyperthymesia): first documented by Parker, Cahill & McGaugh 2006, 'A case of unusual autobiographical remembering', Neurocase 12(1). Only a few dozen confirmed cases since ('a rare few').",
    "HSAM individuals can give the day of the week for dates and recall what they did and details of those days (LePort et al. 2012; Parker et al. 2006).",
    "LePort et al. 2012 (Neurobiol Learn Mem 98(1)): HSAM participants did NOT differ from controls on digit span, visual reproduction and word-pair memory; their advantage is specific to autobiographical and public-event memory ('word pairs... like everyone else').",
    "Jill Price (the 2006 case 'AJ') described her memory as 'non-stop, uncontrollable and totally exhausting' and 'a burden' (quoted in Parker et al. 2006).",
    "Illustrative (labelled on screen): WHICH days a normal memory keeps (random landmarks + the last few weeks) and which days are 'bad' are seeded choices, not data."
  ],
